 ## Background
-The method originates from the adaptation of 3D Gaussian Splatting [3D Gaussian Splatting](1795-3d-gaussian-splatting.md) to X-ray imaging, where the physical model of light interaction (reflection/emission) is replaced by X-ray attenuation (absorption/scattering) [S1]. Standard 3DGS assumes view-dependent appearance, which is invalid for X-rays where attenuation is path-integrated and isotropic [Radiative Gaussian Splatting](3040-radiative-gaussian-splatting.md). This family enables differentiable rendering of X-ray projections, allowing for gradient-based optimization of 3D density fields from 2D projections [Radiative Gaussian Splatting](3040-radiative-gaussian-splatting.md).
